SECTION 4 - LOCAL OPERATION AND DATA

The Software is designed to perform its analysis locally on the User's system.
The Author does not intentionally transmit scanned data, reports, credentials,
process information, registry data, environment data, or system metadata to the
Author or to a remote service.

The Software may create local reports, cache files, temporary files, and
configuration access records as part of its normal operation. It does not
intentionally modify game processes, game files, Windows services, drivers, or
registry values.

The User is responsible for reviewing the permissions required by the Software
and for complying with the laws and policies applicable to the User's system.


SECTION 5 - REPORTS AND CONFIDENTIALITY

Generated reports may contain sensitive information, including user paths,
process names, service names, registry values, environment information, network
information, hashes, file metadata, and digital-signature subjects.

The User is solely responsible for protecting, storing, sharing, publishing,
and deleting generated reports. The Author makes no representation that report
data is complete, accurate, confidential, or suitable for any particular purpose.

The User shall not publish or distribute a report in a manner that violates
applicable law, privacy obligations, or third-party rights.


SECTION 6 - ADMINISTRATOR PRIVILEGES AND SYSTEM RISK

The Software may request Windows administrator privileges through User Account
Control to inspect protected system data.

The User must run the Software only from a trusted source and must maintain
appropriate backups before using elevated privileges. The User is responsible
for reviewing the output, validating findings, and deciding whether any action
should be taken.

The Author does not guarantee that the Software will be uninterrupted, that all
system locations will be accessible, or that elevated operations will succeed
on every Windows configuration.


SECTION 7 - DETECTION LIMITATIONS

The Software provides heuristic indicators only. A reported result does not
guarantee the presence, absence, identity, safety, ownership, or legal status of
any software, process, driver, service, file, or user.

The Software may produce false positives, false negatives, incomplete results,
or results that vary according to Windows version, permissions, locale, policy,
hardware, installed software, and historical artifacts.

Results must be correlated with independent forensic, administrative, legal,
and security sources before being treated as evidence or used for any decision.


